# Go build / test artifacts
/bin/
/dist/
*.exe
*.test
*.out
cover.out
coverage.*
# coverage.sh is source, not a coverage artifact (would otherwise match coverage.*)
!/scripts/coverage.sh

# Go workspace: go.work is TRACKED — it is what makes the multi-module build
# (root + examples) resolve locally and in CI. Only the generated sum is ignored.
#
# With drift at zero the workspace needs no go.work.sum at all — verified: delete
# it and `go build` over both modules still exits 0, and it is not recreated.
# scripts/check-module-drift.sh is what keeps drift at zero.
#
# What ignoring it does NOT cost, stated precisely because the first version of
# this comment overstated it: on the path Dependabot actually takes — raise a
# requirement, then `go mod tidy` — the module-ZIP hash of the version compiled
# into the library lands in TRACKED examples/go.sum, so it is in the diff and in
# the tidy step's pathspec. Measured with an examples-only pgx v5.10.0 -> v5.11.0
# plus tidy: the `v5.11.0 h1:` zip hash appears in examples/go.sum and not in the
# root go.sum, and the go.work.sum such a run generates held only `/go.mod`
# hashes — module-graph metadata, no compilable code. A bare `go mod edit` with
# no tidy is the case where the pin would be untracked, and it is not a shape any
# tool here produces.
go.work.sum

